22:| ADR-018 | Accepted | Pin Sparkle 2.9.4 exactly in `ReluxProxyMac`; require EdDSA-signed payloads plus a signed appcast with pre-extraction verification and no failure expiry; publish only final Developer ID-signed, hardened-runtime, notarized/stapled DMGs; use default stable plus opt-in `prerelease` items on the public HTTPS feed; replace/activate the direct-distribution packet-tunnel system extension only after host relaunch; use higher-build forward rollback because Sparkle 2 has no downgrade path; iOS stays with the App Store |
24:| ADR-020 | Accepted | Set HEV `udp-copy-buffer-nums` M0 baseline to 2 (injectable), so the effective task stack stays 24576; the pinned HEV computes task stack = 20480 + max(tcp-buffer-size, 1500 × udp-copy-buffer-nums) and the default 10 silently forces 35480. Final value is an M3 physical-UDP evidence gate; HEV stays unmodified (config only). Resolves the TASK-260715-1vv52g stop-the-line. |
26:| ADR-022 | Proposed | Require an ordered, explicit per-profile `dnsResolver` containing a non-empty list of numeric IPv4/IPv6 DNS endpoints; select generation-scoped DNS-over-TCP through authenticated SSH for M1 and the same endpoints for M2 relay UDP with explicitly bounded TCP retry. There is no Relux/product resolver default, exit-host discovery, hostname resolver endpoint, tunneled DoH, or physical-resolver fallback in the baseline. TASK-260715-1tnjlu owns schema and failure invariants. TASK-260721-3miqh4 proves the exact 65,535-byte DNS / 65,537-byte framed boundary, structural attempts, corrected accounting equations, 20 validator-backed default/hard timing mutations, exact reliability traces, and observed cleanup. Its 4-endpoint/16-owner/4 MiB/35-second candidate default and 8-endpoint/32-owner/8 MiB/135-second candidate envelope are not production-authorized: policy verification requires the exact non-authoritative class, false authorization booleans, blocker IDs, later physical gate, and structural contracts. ADR-014 has no selected-SSH `direct-tcpip` evidence and ADR-009 has no accepted residual DNS component ledger. Machine policy sets `productionAuthorization.permitted=false`; consumers remain blocked until TASK-260715-1gjxer, selected-engine controlled rows, TASK-260715-1pn983, physical provider evidence, and independent architecture review are accepted. |
28:| ADR-023 | Accepted | Scope the M0 SSH transport contract to **viability** (Option A). M0-viability-mandatory: pre-auth raw host-key evidence, approved public-key authentication, `direct-tcpip`, bidirectional exec plus exec/stdin relay upload, client-initiated rekey by byte/time threshold, bounded buffers and backpressure, deterministic cancellation and lifecycle, keepalive, privacy-safe errors, and cheaply-available metrics. Deferred to M3 as explicitly evidence-gated obligations, never silent waivers: (1) consumer-driven receive-window credit with an immutable per-channel cap, (2) the RFC 4254 channel-open rejection reason taxonomy, (3) exact exec-exit metadata distinguishing `status(0)` from `notReported` and exposing `coreDumped`, (4) deep rekey and keepalive observability including server-initiated KEX lifecycle/generation and reply-correlated keepalive RTT/timeout/miss. M0 adapters MUST surface deferred semantics as explicit not-reported/unsupported states. Owner tasks: `TASK-260728-yx2fca` (contract re-scope), `TASK-260728-3cveay` (M3 delivery). Resolves the three-round `TASK-260715-1ozsb6` stop-the-line. |
29:| ADR-024 | Accepted | The prototype physical target is **macOS-only on the current Apple-silicon Mac**. iOS targets, provider, UI, TestFlight, and App Store work are deferred; their identifiers stay defined in the Apple identifier/entitlement matrix so they resume without renaming. Gate P0 is recorded from macOS evidence alone. A Linux CI runner and native Linux relay-asset execution evidence are **not** required for the working-client path; they move to the release path (`TASK-260715-1c4l9v`). Relux Works Apple Development and Developer ID Application **signing identities** are present in the local Keychain. Notarization credentials are **not** yet in a usable Keychain form — see ADR-025. Secrets stay in the Keychain and are never copied to repo, board, logs, or `providerConfiguration`. |
32:| ADR-027 | Accepted | **Deferral is expressed as `blocked` status, not as an unlinked backlog item.** A task deferred by owner decision — Gate A0 research (`TASK-260715-1o3q6l`), further `ReluxNIOSSH` fork work (`TASK-260715-1af33i`), iOS targets (`TASK-260715-33oofa`), physical-iPhone gates (`TASK-260715-1kntdx`) — carries `blocked` status with the evidence packet naming the deciding ADR and the exact input that would resume it. Leaving a deferred task in `backlog` with its blockers removed makes it *schedulable*, which is how prohibited work re-enters an autonomous run. Retained evidence and downstream links are preserved so the branch re-arms unchanged. |
